-- Q3335: Interfund Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["An interfund transfer reported as other financing sources and uses","An interfund reimbursement that corrects a prior period misclassification","An interfund service provided and used, recorded as revenue and expenditure","An interfund loan creating reciprocal receivable and payable balances"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 112, when a proprietary fund provides services to other government funds at its normal billing rate, the transaction is classified as an interfund service provided and used. The enterprise fund recognizes revenue and the general fund records an expenditure, mirroring external transaction treatment.
Wrong (A): A transfer is a nonreciprocal one-way resource movement; this transaction involves an exchange of services for payment.
Wrong (B): A reimbursement corrects costs charged to the wrong fund, not an ongoing service arrangement at normal rates.
Wrong (D): An interfund loan involves temporary borrowing, not an exchange of services for payment.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3335;

-- Q3337: Interfund Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Eliminated during the government-wide consolidation process entirely","Reported as an expense of governmental activities on the statement","Reported as revenue of business-type activities on the statement","Reported separately as transfers in and transfers out on the statement"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 61, transfers between governmental activities and business-type activities are not eliminated on the government-wide statements because they cross activity boundaries. The transfer is reported as a transfer out in governmental activities and a transfer in for business-type activities.
Wrong (A): Cross-activity transfers are not eliminated; only interfund balances within the same activity type are eliminated during consolidation.
Wrong (B): The transfer is not reclassified as an expense; it retains its character as a transfer on the statement of activities.
Wrong (C): The transfer is not reported as revenue; it is shown as a separate transfer-in line item distinct from program or general revenues.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3337;

-- Q3339: Interfund Transactions [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Eliminated during the government-wide consolidation process entirely","Disclosed only in the notes to the financial statements as supplementary detail","Reported as a note receivable and note payable between the two activity types","Reported as an internal balance between governmental and business-type activities"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 58, interfund balances between governmental activities and business-type activities are reported as internal balances on the government-wide statement of net position. These balances are not eliminated because they cross activity-type boundaries.
Wrong (A): Cross-activity balances are not eliminated; only balances within the same activity type are eliminated during consolidation.
Wrong (B): The balance is reported on the face of the statement of net position, not solely in the notes.
