-- Q3340: Interfund Transactions [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["An interfund transfer moving resources permanently to the correct fund","Writing off the overpayment as a miscellaneous expenditure of the period","An interfund reimbursement from the Special Revenue Fund to the General Fund","Recognizing additional revenue in the General Fund to offset the overpayment"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 112, an interfund reimbursement restores costs initially charged to the wrong fund. The Special Revenue Fund reimburses the General Fund, reducing the General Fund''s expenditures while recording the cost in the proper fund.
Wrong (A): A transfer is a policy-based nonreciprocal resource movement, not a correction of a misclassified expenditure.
Wrong (B): Writing off the overpayment would leave the cost in the wrong fund and fail to correct the misclassification.
Wrong (D): Recognizing revenue is incorrect because a reimbursement is a cost correction, not an income-generating event.$EXPL$
