-- Q3341: Interfund Transactions [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Eliminated to the extent it creates a profit margin above actual cost","Left as reported because internal service funds are self-sustaining entities","Reported as miscellaneous revenue of the internal service fund operations","Charged against the internal service fund''s unrestricted net position"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 61, internal service fund charges that exceed actual cost create internal profits that must be eliminated on the government-wide financial statements. The 10% markup inflates both expenses and revenues, which does not represent an arm''s-length external transaction.
Wrong (B): Leaving overcharges as reported would overstate the government''s actual cost of operations on government-wide statements.
Wrong (C): The overcharge is not miscellaneous revenue; it is an internal markup that must be eliminated in consolidation.
