Wrong (C): Waiting for resolution is not required; ASC 805 requires recognition at acquisition date when fair value is determinable.
Wrong (D): Contingent liabilities are recognized in business combinations when fair value can be measured, unlike the general ASC 450 framework.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3367;

-- Q3371: Advanced Consolidations [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Proceeds minus the original purchase price paid at acquisition date","Proceeds minus the subsidiary''s book value of equity at date of sale","Fair value of proceeds minus the fair value of net assets retained","Proceeds minus the carrying amount of the investment on an equity method basis"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): The gain or loss on disposal of a subsidiary equals proceeds received minus the carrying amount of the parent''s investment at the disposal date on an equity method basis, including unamortized fair value adjustments and goodwill. This reflects the parent''s net interest in the subsidiary.
Wrong (A): The original purchase price ignores subsequent equity method adjustments, share of earnings, dividends, and amortization of basis differences.
Wrong (B): The subsidiary''s book value of equity does not include fair value adjustments and goodwill recognized by the parent at acquisition.
Wrong (C): This formula conflates fair value measurement with carrying amount; the investment is measured at its equity method carrying amount, not remeasured to fair value.$EXPL$
