  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB Statement No. 14, a primary government is a state government, general purpose local government, or special purpose government that has a separately elected governing body, is legally separate, and is fiscally independent. All three criteria must be met for special purpose governments to qualify.
Wrong (B): Receiving and distributing federal funding does not define a primary government; the definition centers on governance, legal separation, and fiscal independence.
Wrong (C): Primary governments include cities, counties, and qualifying special purpose governments — not only state-level entities that issue bonds.
